JAVASCRIPT LOGIC-BUILDING PRACTICE
Intermediate to Advanced Questions and CLI Projects
Repository: javascript-learning-development-journey

Purpose
--------
Build problem-solving skills through practice. Solve each task independently, test edge cases,
and upload your own solutions to GitHub. These questions intentionally contain NO solutions.

Suggested folder structure
--------------------------
javascript-learning-development-journey/
  README.md
  conditionals/
  loops/
  number-logic/
  functions/
  strings/
  arrays/
  cli-projects/

General rules
-------------
1. Use clear variable names and consistent formatting.
2. Validate user input where appropriate.
3. Test normal, boundary, invalid, and unusual inputs.
4. Do not use a shortcut when a question explicitly forbids it.
5. For CLI projects, use Node.js and the terminal. Use prompt-sync or another input
   package only if you have learned how to install and use packages; otherwise use a
   simple Node-compatible input approach you understand.
6. Commit work in small steps and write a short README for each project.

